# Driver App Technical Architecture (Flutter BLoC + Laravel + PostgreSQL)

## 1. Architecture Design
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Driver App (Flutter)] --> B[BLoC + Repositories]
    B --> C[Laravel API (REST)]
    C --> D[(PostgreSQL)]
    C --> E[File Storage (Hetzner/local/S3-compatible)]
    A --> F[Google Maps SDK + Directions API]
    A --> G[Device Services: Camera, GPS, Network]
    C --> H[Realtime (WebSocket/Pusher) (optional)]
```

## 2. Technology Description (Aligned with your existing project)
- Mobile: Flutter + BLoC (flutter_bloc), feature-based architecture (`data/domain/presentation`)
- Backend: Laravel (REST API), authentication via Sanctum or JWT (match your current setup)
- Database: PostgreSQL
- Hosting: Hetzner server (Laravel API + queue workers + scheduler)
- Maps/Tracking: Google Maps SDK (Flutter) + Google Directions/Geocoding APIs
- Offline sync: Reuse existing Hive local database pattern (already used in Store Keeper module)

## 3. Driver App Route Definitions (Flutter)
These are in-app routes/screens (not HTTP routes):
| Screen | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Driver Dashboard | Current trip, lifecycle status, alerts, earnings summary |
| Pickup Scan | Scan product at factory (4A) |
| Delivery Scan | Scan at delivery location; button only within 100m (4B-4C) |
| Location Confirm | Recipient confirmation fallback to unlock scan (4D) |
| Proof of Delivery | PIN / recipient-with-doc photo / digital signature (4E, 4R) |
| Map Tracking | Live navigation + tracking (4F) |
| Earnings | Salary/commission/bonus/trip fee breakdown (4G) |
| Payment History | Previous payments + invoice download (4H) |
| Vehicle Info | Vehicle + plate number (4I) |
| Meter Readings | Start, delivery, return (4J) |
| Expenses | Fuel/food/mechanic/other receipts + amounts (4K-4O) |
| Chat | Driver ↔ Admin, Driver ↔ Recipient (4P, 4X) |
| Compliance | License/insurance/registration expiry (4Y) |

## 4. API Definitions (Laravel)
All endpoints are served by Laravel and secured by driver auth.

### 4.1 Trip lifecycle
Update trip status (enforce forward-only transitions)
```
POST /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/status
```
Request JSON:
| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|------|------|----------|------|
| status | string | yes | Assigned/Picked-Up/In-Transit/Arrived/Delivered/Completed |
| lat | number | yes | Current latitude |
| lng | number | yes | Current longitude |
| device_time | string | no | ISO8601 |
| client_event_id | string | yes | Idempotency key for offline sync |

### 4.2 Delivery scan eligibility (100m + recipient override)
```
GET /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/delivery-scan-eligibility
```
Response JSON:
| Field | Type | Notes |
|------|------|------|
| scan_allowed | boolean | True if within 100m OR recipient override exists |
| distance_m | number | Server-calculated distance |
| reason | string | e.g. OUTSIDE_GEOFENCE, GPS_DISABLED, SPOOFING_SUSPECTED |

### 4.3 Pickup and delivery scans
```
POST /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/scan/pickup
POST /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/scan/delivery
```
Request JSON:
| Field | Type | Required |
|------|------|----------|
| code | string | yes |
| lat | number | yes |
| lng | number | yes |
| client_event_id | string | yes |

### 4.4 Proof of delivery (POD)
```
POST /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/pod
```
Multipart form-data:
| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|------|------|----------|------|
| verification_type | string | yes | pin/photo/signature |
| pin | string | conditional | Required when verification_type=pin |
| recipient_photo | file | conditional | Required when verification_type=photo |
| recipient_document_photo | file | conditional | Required when verification_type=photo |
| signature_image | file | conditional | Required when verification_type=signature |
| recipient_name | string | yes | |

### 4.5 Expenses (fuel/food/mechanic/other)
```
POST /api/v1/driver/trips/{tripId}/expenses
```
Multipart form-data:
| Field | Type | Required |
|------|------|----------|
| type | string | yes |
| amount | number | yes |
| receipt | file | yes |
| notes | string | no |

### 4.6 Chat and archival
Chat can be implemented with standard REST + polling first, and upgraded to WebSockets later.
```
GET  /api/v1/driver/chats
GET  /api/v1/driver/chats/{chatId}/messages
POST /api/v1/driver/chats/{chatId}/messages
```

